    "CanonicalTensorCoordinatesR4 constructs the product-coordinate isometry on the existing TensorHilbert(n+1), with n=0 denoting one particle. The vacuum, symmetric restriction and Fock sum are distinct subsequent steps. Coordinate order is prior index then new rapidity, with pure formula f(p.2) tensor v(p.1).",
